Usage (also as `operator` or `ai`):
  seeker-ai                      agent chat (with tools), saved after every step and resumable
  seeker-ai --chat               conversation only, no tools
  seeker-ai "task"               one shot          seeker-ai --resume       continue the last chat
  seeker-ai -f FILE "question"   attach files (repeatable); piped stdin is attached too
  seeker-ai --models             models in ~/models (* = default)
  seeker-ai --use NAME           make a model the default (any part of its file name)
  seeker-ai --model NAME "..."   use a model for this run only
  seeker-ai --remote             use the model of config key "remote" (e.g. the Mac through `adb reverse`), not the phone's
  seeker-ai --start | --stop | --status
  seeker-ai --serve              the ZION ZERO launcher's "ai" screen, as a background service (Termux's job scheduler)
  seeker-ai --task "goal"        plan the goal, run it step by step, keep the progress on disk, end with a report
  seeker-ai --task-resume [ID]   go on with an interrupted task (the last one)      seeker-ai --tasks   list them
  seeker-ai --task --unattended  nobody at the terminal (zion, the supervisor): the owner's policy decides, and what it
                                 says to approve parks the task until he approves it himself (exit 4); --policy prints it
In a chat: /file PATH  /tools  /memory  /forget  /history  /resume [N]  /system  /reset  /exit   Ctrl+C stops an answer.
Config: ~/.config/seeker-ai/config.json   Instructions: ~/.config/seeker-ai/system.md (optional, replaces the default)
Policy for unattended work: ~/.config/zion/policy.json   Emergency stop: ~/.local/state/zion/STOP (zion-stop, the launcher)
Data: ~/.local/share/seeker-ai/ (memory.md, sessions/, tasks/, history.jsonl, perf.jsonl, changes.tsv, server.log)
Cache: ~/.cache/seeker-ai/slots/ (the instructions + tools part of the prompt, computed once: first answer in ~1 s)"""
